[Music]  there were a lot of surprises this year  I played a lot of games that I didn't  know we're going to be as amazing as  they ended up being and one of those  wonderful surprises this year was soma  it's from the same developers as amnesia  Dark Descent so you'd imagine it to be  this super terrifying immersive horror  experience but soma is something else  something completely unexpected I don't  I don't want to give away too much but  it's incredibly immersive imagine  Bioshock but you get to go out into the  water and explore the underwater world  so you're kind of in this world that  used to be something great it's now  completely destroyed it's absolutely  beautiful and I love the water life I  love exploring the world but most  importantly and what really stuck with  me was concept of humanity and what it  means to be human the next one on my  list is not so much of a surprise  because I played this at different  places throughout the year and I've been  looking forward to it since the initial  reboot a few years ago it's Tomb Raider  and rise of the Tomb Raider and this  game is expectedly great I thought it  was gonna be wonderful I really enjoyed  every time I've been able to get my  hands on it and then when the game  actually came out it was what I wanted  you get to raid tombs you get these  great puzzles you get a wonderful  character experience like Lara is my  homegirl and I love the idea of solving  rich puzzles and figuring out these  ancient secrets and then shooting some  bad dudes in the face there's even  combat puzzles so there's this one  experience where you're under the ice  and there's all these dudes around you  and you have to be able to take them out  silently you can't actually come out of  the ice so you're just kind of dropping  them like slides one by one and I love  those tombs I love the puzzles and I  love the combat and I love  easy-easy game on my left so going back  to surprises something that I did not  expect to love as much as I did was a  little game called Ori and the blind  forest  twas a Metroidvania style game that had  so much heart and so much love built  into it I loved Metroid style games and  this is the perfect example of that it's  a hardcore platformer that's disguised  as this adorable cutesy game so you're  playing this lovable little forest  sprite and within the very first opening  moments of the game I compared a lot to  Pixar's up because it's so emotional and  you really fall in love with these  characters but then you find out that it  is actually quite difficult of a  platformer in itself it's just an  all-encompassing good game especially if  you like platformers especially if you  like hardcore platformer Ori and the  blind forest it's an easy win next up is  another story driven surprise and that  was until dawn and what a crazy amount  of twists and surprises within the game  but also the game itself I had no idea I  was going to enjoy it as much as I did  just super enjoyed both loving and  hating these characters and thus trying  to save them and feeling terrible when  they died or not caring about them and  basically letting them die and it was  just this awesome power this like crazy  wielding of power of letting people  basically go to their deaths making  decisions that I knew would end in their  doom I thought it was really well done  and it just blew me away there's not a  game that came out this year that  touched my heart quite like rocket  League did  and that's why it's my favorite game of  2015 it's truly just gameplay perfection  I don't even really enjoy sports games  but I love rocket League I love how easy  it was to pick up but how much I've  learned over the course of playing this  game throughout the last few months  they've just unlocked all these  different modes there's all these  awesome items that you can pick up from  you know different hats or different  tails or different paint jobs to keep  you coming back there's always a reason  to come back I love everything about  this game and what's wonderful about it  is you don't need that much  you don't need deep immersive plots or  complicated rules or stupid sexy  witcher's all you need is a giant ball  and rocket powered battle cars that's  all you need it is a tremendous  perfection of a video game and I am  honored and stoked to tell you guys that  rocket league is the best game that came  out in 2015  [Music]

